{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5Kz74LNc5NGosJy3xM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `addMonths` in `dates.js`. Customers billed on the 31st will now land on the last day of shorter months instead of spilling into the next month.\n\n**The bug:** `setMonth` doesn't clamp the day. Jan 31 + 1 month became Feb 31, which rolls over to Mar 3.\n\n**The fix:** The function now works out the target year and month, then sets the day to the smaller of the original day and that month's length. The time of day is kept, the input date is never mutated, and negative `n` and year rollover (Dec 31 + 1, Jan 31 − 1) are handled.\n\nI checked these by hand against the code, not by running them, since Bash was denied in this session:\n- Jan 31 2026 + 1 → Feb 28 2026\n- Jan 31 2024 + 1 → Feb 29 2024 (leap year)\n- Mar 31 + 1 → Apr 30\n- Dec 31 2026 + 1 → Jan 31 2027\n- Jan 31 2026 − 1 → Dec 31 2025\n- Jan 15 2026 + 1 → Feb 15 2026 (the example in the file's header comment)\n\nI haven't added a test file or run the existing test suite. If you want the Bash-based check run, you'll need to re-enable Bash or run `node -e` on the file yourself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":853,"cache_read_input_tokens":23791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":853},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24a4af05-b9ba-40a7-8453-c6c06e1934bf","uuid":"9465bd48-143e-413c-a134-284a7ac93ad5","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:31:50.272Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5KyxNQHEAgESFXzgXU"}
